{"id": "22079", "revid": "2253620", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=22079", "title": "Mesopotamia (Argentina)", "text": "Mesopotamia is a region in the northeast of Argentina bordered to the north by Paraguay, to the east by Brazil and Uruguay, to the south and west by the Pampas region, and in the northwest by the Chaco region.\nLike its ancient eponym in the Middle East, the region is dominated by two rivers: the Paran\u00e1 and the Uruguay, in this case.\nRegions.\nThe following provinces are considered part of Mesopotamia:\nGet in.\nBy plane.\nCorrientes, Posadas and Puerto Iguaz\u00fa have airports with flights to Buenos Aires. Check Aerol\u00edneas Argentinas[dead link] and Fly Bondi[dead link].\nBy bus.\nFrequent connections between Posadas, Corrientes, Rosario and Buenos Aires."}
